  <prompt>Port NamingConformanceScriptRunner (naming-conformance-check.ps1, 200 lines; 0 az/REST calls -- pure local string/convention checks per DS-4 §6) to a trivial pure-C# INamingConformanceChecker implementation. This is the second-easiest probe in the H13 suite after I1 (task 170) -- no live Azure dependency at all.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in trivial pure-function ports (string/naming-convention checks, no I/O).</role>

  <goal>INamingConformanceChecker exists as a pure C# port of naming-conformance-check.ps1's convention rules, with zero Azure SDK/REST dependency. Given a resource-name string violating the canonical naming convention (per docs/architecture/AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md), it returns Fail; given a conformant name, Pass.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §6 explicitly notes this script makes '0 az/REST calls' -- the entire port is a pure-function string/regex-rules translation, the same convention rules this project's Phase G (tasks 018-021, already ✅) already baked into provisioning-time naming.</background>
